<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Construction Payroll?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Salary processing and statutory compliance for multi-layered construction workforce: permanent staff wages, contractor payroll verification (EPF/ESI/min wages), BOCW cess, multi-site attendance, TDS, and inter-state migrant worker compliance. For <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>For Gurugram developers with 5-20 active sites and 10-20 contractors each: daily compliance operation involving thousands of workers and multiple govt authorities (EPFO/ESIC/BOCW/Labour Dept). For <a href="/tds-return-filing-24q">TDS Return Filing</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Construction Payroll:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>BOCW Cess:</strong> 1% of project cost to Haryana BOCW Welfare Board. 10+ workers. Delays OC if unpaid</li><li><strong>Principal Employer Liability:</strong> Developer liable for contractor workers' EPF/ESI. Back-demand if contractor defaults</li><li><strong>Contractor Verification:</strong> Check EPF ECR + ESI + min wages before payment release</li><li><strong>50% Wage Rule (SSC 2020):</strong> Basic min 50% CTC. Increases PF/ESI base. Effective Nov 2025</li><li><strong>ECR:</strong> Electronic Challan-cum-Return for EPF. Monthly by 15th. 1%/month interest on delay</li><li><strong>OSH Code Migrant:</strong> Displacement allowance 50% wages (min Rs 1,000) for inter-state workers</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
